|game_text=Plays on table. At end of a turn, if opponent has 15 or more cards in hand, may use 2 Force to shuffle all but 9 (random selection) into Used Pile. If Grimtaash or Thrown Back just targeted your hand, may reveal 2 cards from hand; they cannot be removed or checked for duplicates.
|errata_history=This is the original printing: the earliest PC card image of this card (11 December 2022). It is not the current version; the current version is [[Drop! (V) (Errata)]] (PC-E1). The image is the PC card image of this version.
* '''Original''' (this page): PC card image of 11 December 2022<ref name="ht-D_drop-0">PC card image in the PC's Holotable image set: [https://github.com/swccgpc/holotable/blob/23a3730/Images-HT/starwars/Virtual20-Dark/large/drop.gif drop.gif], commit [https://github.com/swccgpc/holotable/commit/23a3730 23a3730] (11 December 2022, “Fixing case and making gifs”); high-resolution image <code>Virtual20-Dark/hires/drop.png</code>, commit [https://github.com/swccgpc/holotable/commit/711a663 711a663] (11 December 2022, “Set 20 New Cards and Luke AI”).</ref>, no errata mark; lower-left name “Drop!”. Published the day before [[Virtual Set 20]] was released (12 December 2022) and unchanged at release, so it is the original (not a playtest image). Text: “Plays on table. At end of a turn, if opponent has 15 or more cards in hand, may use 2 Force to shuffle all but 9 (random selection) into Used Pile. If Grimtaash or Thrown Back just targeted your hand, may reveal 2 cards from hand; they cannot be removed or checked for duplicates.”
* '''PC-E1''' ([[Drop! (V) (Errata)]]): PC card image of 22 July 2024<ref name="ht-D_drop-1">PC card image in the PC's Holotable image set: [https://github.com/swccgpc/holotable/blob/6c22b09/Images-HT/starwars/Virtual20-Dark/large/drop.gif drop.gif], commit [https://github.com/swccgpc/holotable/commit/6c22b09 6c22b09] (22 July 2024, “Fixing case and making gifs”); high-resolution image <code>Virtual20-Dark/hires/drop.png</code>, commit [https://github.com/swccgpc/holotable/commit/a546b30 a546b30] (21 July 2024, “Set 23 Errata”).</ref>, marked “E1”; lower-left name “Drop!”. What changed from the previous version: PC errata released with [[Virtual Set 23]] and the July 2024 Defensive Shield Update Kit<ref name="dskit2024">Players Committee, [https://res.starwarsccg.org/virtual/DShieldUpdateKit_2024_July.pdf July 2024 Defensive Shield Update Kit] (PDF, 3 pages, “SWCCG Players Committee, July 2024”; file built 2 August 2024), released with [[Virtual Set 23]] (22 July 2024).</ref> (image marked “E1”): “use 2 Force” becomes “use 3 Force” and “reveal 2 cards” becomes “reveal 3 cards”. Text: “Plays on table. At end of a turn, if opponent has 15 or more cards in hand, may use 3 Force to shuffle all but 9 (random selection) into Used Pile. If Grimtaash or Thrown Back just targeted your hand, may reveal 3 cards from hand; they cannot be removed or checked for duplicates.”
Versions follow Bill's rulings of 12 November 2026: every visible change on a PC card image is a version, numbered in release order; a printed errata mark that does not match that order is recorded as a PC transcription error.
